Control Plane Components
kube-apiserver: The single REST API entry point for the entire cluster. It handles authentication, authorization (RBAC), admission control, and is the only component that writes to etcd.

etcd: A distributed, consistent key-value store acting as the single source of truth for the desired and actual cluster state[cite: 2].

kube-scheduler: Continuously monitors for unassigned Pods and evaluates node conditions (capacity, taints, affinity) to select the optimal node[cite: 2].

kube-controller-manager: Contains internal reconciliation loops (Deployment Controller, EndpointSlice Controller, Node Controller) that drive actual cluster state toward the desired state declared in manifests[cite: 2].

Worker Node Components
kubelet: The node-level agent that communicates directly with kube-apiserver[cite: 2]. It watches for Pods assigned to its node and issues Container Runtime Interface (CRI) instructions[cite: 2].

Container Runtime (e.g., containerd): Low-level engine responsible for pulling images, allocating cgroups and network namespaces, and running containers[cite: 2].

kube-proxy: The network proxy running on each node that maintains network rules (iptables or IPVS) to distribute traffic destined for Service virtual IPs across healthy Pod backends.